And now, we return to the present.

253
00:17:20,280 --> 00:17:21,420
Hey, Luffy!

254
00:17:21,900 --> 00:17:24,180
We can set sail whenever you're ready!

255
00:17:25,360 --> 00:17:26,220
All right.

256
00:17:26,780 --> 00:17:29,737
But are you really sure you
want to leave like this?

257
00:17:29,820 --> 00:17:32,377
We didn't say goodbye
to Momo or to Kinamon.

258
00:17:32,460 --> 00:17:34,957
Seems kind of wrong after all
we've been through with them.

259
00:17:35,040 --> 00:17:36,393
She's right, as always.

260
00:17:37,140 --> 00:17:37,970
They'll be fine.

261
00:17:38,053 --> 00:17:39,797
If Luffy wants to go, let's go.

262
00:17:39,880 --> 00:17:42,097
Why you gotta be such a bastard, Mosshead?

263
00:17:42,180 --> 00:17:44,840
Screw off, curly brows. Hey! What?

264
00:17:47,620 --> 00:17:48,450
Although,

265
00:17:48,533 --> 00:17:50,977
it is a bit of a shame since
we shared so many adventures

266
00:17:51,060 --> 00:17:53,937
with those two even before
we came to the land of Wano.

267
00:17:54,020 --> 00:17:57,314
It does feel a bit cold to
silently sail away like this.

268
00:18:02,480 --> 00:18:04,900
Well, Luffy, you can make the call.

269
00:18:10,760 --> 00:18:11,940
Don't worry, guys.

270
00:18:12,320 --> 00:18:13,520
He'll be here soon.
